  "slug": "visualization-gfaidx-7f7d",
  "summary": "Scalable 3D-aware search now reaches nucleic acid structures and genome-scale and viral structure collections.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is structure-level retrieval and comparison that goes beyond sequence similarity. RFoldSearch encodes RNA structure with a learned 80-state structural alphabet (3Dr) and uses indexed search for fast, sensitive retrieval. RNAhub2 targets scale, adding query-adapted prefiltering, parallel resumable genome searches, and NAF compression for structure-based RNA homology discovery. GTalign extends 3D structure search and alignment to RNA and DNA, reporting higher TM-score accuracy than benchmarked tools. BFVD v3 complements these with a database of ColabFold-AlphaFold2-predicted viral protein structures. What is new is the combination of a structural alphabet, indexing, and compression that makes structure-based search across large nucleic acid and genome-scale collections tractable, rather than the development of structure predictors themselves.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
